\0
As the Freedom Guard grew in military strength, their political influence increased as well. The Freedom Guard negotiated a treaty with several outlying provincial governments, only marginally under Imperium control. This Pax Liberati, which was to be signed at a conference on Lycean, would significantly improve their strategic position in the outlying sectors and increase the Freedom Guard's access to critical resources.\n\n
The Imperium was aware of the summit but did not wish to cement the alliance by attacking the involved worlds. Instead they duplicated a division of Freedom Guard troops and stormed Lycean in an attempt to make the conference appear to be a Freedom Guard ambush and splinter the coalition.
\1
The Imperium has launched an offensive on the city of Lycean, where the Pax Liberati is being signed. The Imperium has duplicated a squadron of our own units and is attacking the city with them, presumably in an attempt to make the conference appear to be an ambush on our part. Intercept the impostors and eliminate them before they can destroy the city. The treaty will be signed in 30 minutes, so you must hold out until then. 
\n\n
\cOBJECTIVES\n
\n
-->  Protect the civilian city for 30 minutes, \n
\s\s\s\s after which the treaty will be signed\n 
-->  Destroy the enemy HQ which houses the\n
\s\s\s\s stolen plans
\2
Your excellence is noted. Carry on.\n
\n
\cHISTORICAL OUTCOME:\n
The Freedom Guard sentry force patrolling Lycean during the conference was surprised by the attack with their own vehicles and reacted slowly to the onslaught. The masquerading Imperium force devastated the town, murdering numerous civilians and even killing two ambassadors who were negotiating with the Freedom Guard. The Pax Liberati was never signed, and the Freedom Guard never marshaled  control of the outlying provinces.
\3
I have doubts of your competence.
